Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 3 — Flutter Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand Flutter applications. Flutter applications differ fundamentally from traditional Android apps because most application logic is written in Dart and rendered by the Flutter engine rather than the Android View system. By the end of this section, you should be able to reconstruct a Flutter application's architecture, execution model, widget hierarchy, state management, native integration, and runtime behavior.



> Core Principle:
Flutter applications are Android hosts for a Dart runtime. Reverse engineer the Dart application first, then understand how it interacts with Android.




