Stage 31 — Common Flutter Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating Flutter like a traditional Android View application.

Spending excessive time on the Android bootstrap code before understanding the Dart application.

Confusing widgets with rendered objects.

Ignoring state management architecture.

Treating every rebuild as business logic.

Overlooking Platform Channels and plugin boundaries.

Assuming Java/Kotlin contains the application's core logic.



---

Stage 32 — Flutter APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify and profile Flutter-based Android applications.

✅ Reconstruct Flutter architecture from the Android host through the Dart runtime to the rendering pipeline.

✅ Recover widget hierarchies, navigation, state management, and asynchronous execution models.

✅ Understand isolates, streams, futures, and the Flutter event loop.

✅ Trace communication between Dart and Android through Platform Channels and plugins.

✅ Distinguish engine infrastructure, framework code, plugin code, and handwritten application logic.

✅ Correlate static reconstruction with runtime behavior to validate execution and state changes.

✅ Produce comprehensive architectural documentation explaining both the Flutter application and its interaction with the Android platform.



